  "query_preview": "..\n(Monday Night through next Saturday) \nIssued at 1125 AM CDT Sat Sep 26 2026\n\nAs we get into Tuesday, the big storm in New England will start \nto pull off into eastern Canada opening the door for high \npressure to move our way. Afternoon temperatures will respond to \nthis increased ridging by warming well above normal mid to late \nweek. \n\nSmall rain chances will creep into the forecast, but I would not \ncount on much drought relief through Friday. The pattern through \nFriday looks dry for most of us and models are not consistent. \nRain chances do look much better next weekend, and some models \nshow a widespread soaking rainfall. But, other models do not, so \nwe will just have to wait and see if we can look forward to some much-\nneeded rainfall.",
